#: ../source/notebooks/general/prior_predictive.ipynb:10003
#: 0fdfe0d7650e44d2986d1d8ec529425c
msgid "Prior Predictive Modeling"
msgstr "Modelado Predictivo Anterior"

#: ../source/notebooks/general/prior_predictive.ipynb:10005
#: b6ae9d37d2ff46e79ffb095243985568
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"This guide provides an introduction to prior predictive modeling using "
"PyMC (and PyMC-Marketing) and the {class}`Prior "
"<pymc_extras.prior.Prior>` class from PyMC-Marketing.  We start by "
"looking into a simpler example and then we will see how to apply to real "
"case scenarios with marketing mix models in PyMC-Marketing."
msgstr ""
"Esta guía proporciona una introducción a la modelización predictiva previa "
"utilizando PyMC (y PyMC-Marketing) y la clase {class}`Prior "
"<pymc_extras.prior.Prior>` de PyMC-Marketing.  Comenzamos examinando un "
"ejemplo más simple y luego veremos cómo aplicarlo a escenarios de casos "
"reales con modelos de mezcla de marketing en PyMC-Marketing."

#: ../source/notebooks/general/prior_predictive.ipynb:10008
#: 1d86b25b51b14919b405aeb6e942b9e4
msgid ""
"Before diving into the technical details, let's understand why priors are"
" crucial in Bayesian analysis and their practical importance in industry "
"applications."
msgstr ""
"Antes de profundizar en los detalles técnicos, comprendamos por qué los "
"priors son cruciales en el análisis bayesiano y su importancia práctica "
"en las aplicaciones industriales."

#: ../source/notebooks/general/prior_predictive.ipynb:10010
#: b93b431fb94b45c4a7702746a76d86f4
msgid "Understanding Bayesian Inference"
msgstr "Comprendiendo la Inferencia Bayesiana"

#: ../source/notebooks/general/prior_predictive.ipynb:10012
#: 584abf7bddb1457b995e7362c0b134bc
msgid ""
"Bayesian inference is based on Bayes' theorem, which provides a formal "
"way to update our beliefs about parameters $\\theta$ (say, saturation or "
"decay rate in a marketing mix models) given observed data $y$:"
msgstr ""
"La inferencia bayesiana se basa en el teorema de Bayes, que proporciona "
"una forma formal de actualizar nuestras creencias sobre los parámetros "
"$\\theta$ (por ejemplo, la tasa de saturación o de decaimiento en modelos"
" de mezcla de marketing) dado los datos observados $y$:"

#: ../source/notebooks/general/prior_predictive.ipynb:10014
#: 95f12eabefea42edbb9ffd985d206425
#, python-brace-format
msgid "p(\\theta|y) = \\frac{p(y|\\theta)p(\\theta)}{p(y)}"
msgstr "p(\\theta|y) = \\frac{p(y|\\theta)p(\\theta)}{p(y)}"

#: ../source/notebooks/general/prior_predictive.ipynb:10016
#: 5177743fd7904c19ac08dc848bf4c058
msgid "Where:"
msgstr "Dónde:"

#: ../source/notebooks/general/prior_predictive.ipynb:10017
#: e64e9cc691c64491b468fa56eb848915
msgid "$p(\\theta|y)$ is the posterior probability (what we want to learn)"
msgstr "$p(\\theta|y)$ es la probabilidad posterior (lo que queremos aprender)"

#: ../source/notebooks/general/prior_predictive.ipynb:10018
#: 62c0540543c54748968d8977b2fa9cb0
msgid "$p(y|\\theta)$ is the likelihood (how the data is generated)"
msgstr "$p(y|\\theta)$ es la verosimilitud (cómo se generan los datos)"

#: ../source/notebooks/general/prior_predictive.ipynb:10019
#: f37cb9f0c23f4a05bdc1d9af314e2956
msgid "$p(\\theta)$ is the prior probability (our initial beliefs)"
msgstr "$p(\\theta)$ es la probabilidad a priori (nuestras creencias iniciales)"

#: ../source/notebooks/general/prior_predictive.ipynb:10020
#: b0149737f2014df28aa7f9a9f6a86a7e
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"$p(y)$ is the evidence (a normalizing constant), which can be written as "
"$p(y) = \\displaystyle{ \\int p(y|\\theta)p(\\theta)d\\theta }$"
msgstr ""
"$p(y)$ es la evidencia (una constante de normalización), que se puede "
"escribir como $p(y) = \\displaystyle{ \\int "
"p(y|\\theta)p(\\theta)d\\theta }$"

#: ../source/notebooks/general/prior_predictive.ipynb:10022
#: e9015cdab3df4ddca1df2cf18121f05c
msgid ""
"The posterior distribution combines our prior knowledge with the observed"
" data to give us updated beliefs about the parameters. In practice, we "
"often work with the unnormalized posterior:"
msgstr ""
"La distribución posterior combina nuestro conocimiento previo con los "
"datos observados para proporcionarnos creencias actualizadas sobre los "
"parámetros. En la práctica, a menudo trabajamos con la posterior no "
"normalizada:"

#: ../source/notebooks/general/prior_predictive.ipynb:10024
#: 231c46df96e64a1e8b0c5293639f9aae
msgid "p(\\theta|y) \\propto p(y|\\theta)p(\\theta)"
msgstr "p(\\theta|y) \\propto p(y|\\theta)p(\\theta)"

#: ../source/notebooks/general/prior_predictive.ipynb:10026
#: 32a177bbd0194b6eb3bd59bcfef5151b
msgid ""
"This is because the normalizing constant $p(y)$ is often intractable to "
"compute directly."
msgstr ""
"Esto se debe a que la constante de normalización $p(y)$ a menudo es "
"intractable de calcular directamente."

